## Nexus Core — server configuration
##
## Generated by the txAdmin deployment recipe.
##
## Values marked OPERATOR MUST SUPPLY are blank on purpose. Fill them in on your
## server. Never commit a filled-in copy to a repository: a credential in a
## repository is published, and rotation is the only remedy.
##
## RE-RUNNING THE RECIPE DISCARDS EVERY EDIT YOU MAKE HERE.
##
## txAdmin deploys into a NEW data directory each time and regenerates this file
## from the template. The previous directory, and everything you changed in it,
## is gone. Observed on 2026-08-02: a changed listen port survived exactly until
## the next deployment, and the symptom was the server list querying the old port
## with nothing to say why.
##
## Before redeploying, keep a copy of at least: the endpoint ports below, the
## database connection string, the token signing key, and nxc_server_build.

## Listen ports. txAdmin fills these in at deployment, and they must match what
## you have actually port-forwarded — the server list probes the address and port
## the server registers, so a mismatch fails silently with a timeout rather than
## anything that names the port.
{{serverEndpoints}}

sv_hostname "{{serverName}}"
sets sv_projectName "{{serverName}}"
sets sv_projectDesc "{{recipeDescription}}"
sets locale "en-US"
sets tags "roleplay, nexus core, custom framework"

sv_maxclients {{maxClients}}
sv_licenseKey "{{svLicense}}"

## sv_scriptHostBind is NOT set. It does not exist on Enhanced, which rejects it
## at startup with "Command not found (sv_scripthostbind)". Carried over from a
## Legacy template; removed 2026-08-02 after it was observed failing.

set steam_webApiKey "none"

## ------------------------------------------------------------------ platform
## Nexus Core targets FiveM for GTA V ENHANCED and the Enhanced Cfx Server
## runtime. ADR-0016.
##
## THIS RECIPE CANNOT VERIFY WHICH ARTIFACTS YOU INSTALLED. A txAdmin recipe runs
## on a server that already exists; it provisions resources and configuration,
## not the server binary. Deploying this onto a Legacy FXServer will appear to
## succeed and will not be supported.
##
## sv_enforceGameBuild is deliberately absent. It previously pinned 3095, a
## Legacy build, which is how the Legacy default entered this project in the
## first place — nobody chose it. If a build must be enforced on Enhanced, add
## the line with an Enhanced build number; do not restore the old one.

## OPERATOR MUST SUPPLY. The exact Cfx Server build this deployment runs.
##
## Required by MDD v0.4 section 38.2: every deployment records its build, so a
## platform regression can be attributed to a specific update rather than to
## whatever changed most recently. Enhanced is early access; this will happen.
##
## nxc_core refuses to start until this is set. That is deliberate — a value
## that is optional is a value that is empty on the one server where it matters.
##
## WHERE TO FIND IT: the server console prints it on the last line of startup,
## and txAdmin shows it too:
##
##     fx: b106-ea/Win
##          ^^^        build 106, early access, Windows
##
## Enter the number only. This is left BLANK on purpose: a template cannot know
## which build you run, and a pre-filled value is one nobody would correct.
set nxc_server_build ""

## ------------------------------------------------------------------ database
## OPERATOR MUST SUPPLY. Format:
##   mysql://<USER>:<PASSWORD>@<HOST>/<DATABASE>?charset=utf8mb4
## The angle brackets are placeholders. Replace the whole value.
set mysql_connection_string ""

## --------------------------------------------------------------- Nexus Core
## Bootstrap configuration only. Everything operational — business hours,
## payouts, prices, target locations, dispatch rules — is registered by each
## resource and edited in game through a permission-controlled interface.

## Environment identity: development, staging, or production.
set nxc_environment "development"

## Core startup mode: normal or recovery.
set nxc_startup_mode "normal"

## LEAVE THIS BLANK. Nexus Core generates a signing key at every startup, using
## the database's cryptographic random source, and rotates it by restarting.
##
## Restarting therefore invalidates live sessions. That is intended: a session
## token that outlives the server which issued it is a token nobody can revoke.
##
## Set it only if you run more than one server instance that must share sessions.
## A supplied key must be at least 32 characters; a shorter one is refused rather
## than silently replaced.
set nxc_token_signing_key ""

## Log level: debug, info, warn, error. debug is disabled in production.
set nxc_log_level "info"

## Development diagnostics. MUST be false in production: nxc_devtools exposes
## internal state, and a diagnostics tool reachable in production is an
## information-disclosure vulnerability.
set nxc_dev_mode "false"

## The PLATFORM's developer mode, which is a different thing from the line above.
## nxc_dev_mode gates Nexus Core's own diagnostics; sv_devmode gates the Enhanced
## client-side developer tooling, server-wide.
##
## Deliberately left commented out. Server-wide developer mode is subject to the
## platform's player-slot limits and must never be enabled in production
## (MDD v0.4 38.8). Enhanced can also grant it per player through
## deferrals.handover, which is the better route for a shared development server.
# set sv_devmode "true"

## ------------------------------------------------------------------- startup
## Resources start in dependency order. A resource must not assume a later
## resource is available.

ensure mapmanager
ensure spawnmanager

ensure oxmysql

## screenshot-basic is NOT installed. It ships unbuilt — its manifest declares
## dist/client.js, dist/server.js and dist/ui.html, none of which exist in the
## repository — and it builds them through the `yarn` resource, which lives in
## cfx-server-data/[system] and is not part of the Enhanced minimal set.
##
## Observed failing on 2026-08-02: 'Dependency "yarn" failed to load'. Nothing in
## Nexus Core uses it, so it is removed rather than dragged in along with a build
## toolchain of unverified Enhanced compatibility. It returns when a resource
## needs screenshots, with yarn and webpack installed deliberately.

## NO VOICE RESOURCE. pma-voice was removed on 2026-08-02.
##
## Enhanced's voice API is server-side only: the server owns channel membership,
## mute, and deaf state. pma-voice wraps the client-side Mumble natives, which
## are deprecated on Enhanced and work only by routing through the new
## implementation. A client-authoritative voice layer contradicts this
## framework's server-authority rule, and nothing here uses voice yet.
##
## nxc_voice will target the Enhanced server-side API directly.

## Nexus Core foundation. The full order is:
##   nxc_lib -> nexus_core -> nxc_config -> nxc_ui -> nxc_zones -> nxc_target
##   -> nxc_interact -> nxc_devtools
## Only published resources are listed. The rest are added as each is released.

ensure nxc_lib
ensure nxc_core
